<!--
  Regenerated 2026-08-07. Two things were wrong, and the second one mattered more.

  1. ORIGIN. Every <loc> pointed at https://tegridyfarms.vercel.app, which stopped
     being the canonical origin when memetic.fun was declared canonical (index.html's
     <link rel="canonical"> and src/lib/constants.ts SITE_URL). A sitemap on a
     non-canonical origin asks search engines to index the alias.

     RE-POINTED 2026-09-09 to https://memetics.finance. The 2026-08-27 ARRIVAL
     IDENTITY decision (src/lib/constants.ts SITE_URL) moved the canonical host to
     the venue's own name and left memetic.fun as a redirect alias — but this file
     was not moved with it, so for six weeks index.html named one host as canonical
     while the sitemap handed the crawler the whole URL set on the other. That is
     the exact duplicate-content collision item 1 was written about, recreated on a
     different pair of hosts. THE HOST HERE IS NOT EDITED BY HAND: it must equal
     SITE_URL, and src/lib/__tests__/canonicalHost.test.ts fails every <loc> that
     drifts off it.

  2. COVERAGE. Not one Solana route was listed — no /solana, no /solana-launch, no
     /curve-launch. So the crawler-facing product was not merely "framed as"
     Ethereum-only: the Solana pages were never declared to exist. Also missing were
     /launch, /trust, /scan, /deployer and /exposure — the launcher and the whole
     detection suite.

  Deliberately NOT listed: /admin, /art-studio (operator surfaces), /launch/:token
  (per-token permalinks, unbounded and better discovered via the launcher), and the
  routes that render a "not deployed" placeholder today.
-->
